Patch notice: the installed `@executor-js/sdk@1.6.11` bundle is NOT pristine
upstream bytes. One 18-line block was replaced by two lines to remove a
reactive OAuth refresh-and-replay that sent a second upstream business request
after an HTTP 401, bypassing policy, approval, annotation and argument
validation. The patch lives at `patches/@executor-js__sdk@1.6.11.patch`, sha256
e1c1bfa9a41049321f45747f3ae8907d89604fca06872ec0a4871483db1b9fad, and is
applied by pnpm's `patchedDependencies`. The upstream MIT terms and copyright
notice continue to apply to the patched artifact; the modification is recorded
here and in `patches/README.md`. The runtime refuses to enable execution unless
the installed chunk matches the pinned patched digest above.

